{% from "macros.html.j2" import section, plot, tabs %}
{% call section(step, title) %}
  Probabilities come from graph distance to each cluster's peak.
  <b>{{ membership.moved|fmt(',') }}</b> hits are most probable in a different cluster than the
  tree they grew in; from here on a hit's cluster is its most probable one. Hits under 0.5 bits of
  entropy are confident.
{% endcall %}
{% set touching %}
<p class="lede">
  Row = cluster, column = neighbour. Each cell is the share of the cluster's mutual-neighbour
  edges that land in the neighbour. The diagonal is how self-contained a cluster is.
</p>
{{ plot(membership.touching) }}
{% endset %}
{{ tabs("member", [("Entropy", plot(membership.entropy)), ("Which clusters touch", touching)]) }}
